  "interpretation": "<p><strong>COMMENTS:</strong></p>\n<p><br>CALR gene mutation: 30% of cases of PMF have mutations in the CALR gene.<br>This result does not rule out the presence of mutations that may be below the detection limit of the assay.<br>This test detects mutations which are described above only. It does not detect any other mutation.<br>Results are to be interpreted in context of clinical findings other and laboratory data.<br>PCR is a highly sensitive technique, however inherent PCR inhibitors in the specimen can result in<br>amplification failure.</p>\n<p><strong>REFERENCES:</strong></p>\n<p><br>Klamfl T, et al. Somatic mutations of calreticulin in myeloproliferative neoplasms. N Engl J Med 2013; 369:<br>2379-2390.<br>Gold U, et al.Calreticulin: non-endoplasmic reticulum functions in physiology and disease.FASEB J2010; 24:<br>66S-83.</p>",
